  <main id="main-content" class="fade-in">
    <section>
      <p>A rep closed the biggest deal in company history. The celebration was real. The room felt empty.</p>

      <p>Not tired. Not distracted. Empty. The numbers were right and everything underneath them was off.</p>

      <p>That underneath is the whole subject. What a leader carries into the room that nobody asked them to carry. It sets the weather before anyone speaks, and it never shows up on the dashboard.</p>

      <p>Fifteen years leading sales teams before I started paying attention to it. Now Field Notes, twice a month, and a book with <a class="inline-link" href="https://drwarter.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Dr. Carlos Warter</a> on the same question (Park Street Press, 2027).</p>
    </section>

